# Restaurant API

A simple REST API for managing restaurant menu items, built with Node.js and Express.

## Requirements

- Node.js and npm

## Run the server

```bash
npm install
npm start
```

The server listens at `http://localhost:3000`.

## Menu API

All menu endpoints use the `/api/menu` path. For requests with a JSON body, send the `Content-Type: application/json` header.

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GET` | `/api/menu` | Get all menu items. |
| `GET` | `/api/menu/:id` | Get one menu item by ID. |
| `POST` | `/api/menu` | Create a menu item. |
| `PUT` | `/api/menu/:id` | Replace an existing item's editable fields. |
| `PATCH` | `/api/menu/:id` | Update selected fields on an existing item. |
| `DELETE` | `/api/menu/:id` | Delete a menu item. |

### Create or update a menu item

`POST` and `PUT` expect all three fields below. `name` and `description` must be non-empty strings, and `price` must be a positive number.

```json
{
  "name": "BBQ Chicken Pizza",
  "description": "Pizza",
  "price": 250
}
```

Example create request:

```http
POST /api/menu
Content-Type: application/json
```

Example update request:

```http
PUT /api/menu/1
Content-Type: application/json
```

`PUT` replaces the item's `name`, `description`, and `price`; include all fields in the request body.

`PATCH` updates only the fields included in the request body. Include at least one of `name`, `description`, or `price`; each supplied field must be valid. For example, to change only the price:

```http
PATCH /api/menu/1
Content-Type: application/json
```

```json
{
  "price": 275
}
```

## Responses

- Create returns `201 Created` and the new menu item.
- Successful reads and updates return `200 OK` and JSON.
- Delete returns `204 No Content` with an empty response body.
- Invalid request data or IDs return `400 Bad Request`.
- A valid ID that does not match a menu item returns `404 Not Found`.

Menu items are currently stored in memory, so changes are reset when the server restarts.
